WEBVTT

1
00:00:15.844 --> 00:00:16.704
Jacey shouted.

2
00:00:16.724 --> 00:00:18.724
"Brooklyn, watch out!"

3
00:00:19.465 --> 00:00:23.046
Brooklyn tried to move out of the way before Dirk slammed into her.

4
00:00:24.926 --> 00:00:28.387
But he was moving so fast, there was almost nothing she could do.

5
00:00:29.667 --> 00:00:33.164
Dirk crashed into Brooklyn, who crashed into Coach Teagan.

6
00:00:34.205 --> 00:00:39.326
The coach fell down hard on the gym floor while something else flew up into the air.

7
00:00:39.346 --> 00:00:42.767
"My phone!"

8
00:00:43.307 --> 00:00:44.187
the coach cried.

9
00:00:44.207 --> 00:00:47.528
"Ooh!" Dirk rolled on the floor.

10
00:00:49.509 --> 00:00:52.050
Brooklyn tried to get up, a little dazed.

11
00:00:53.790 --> 00:00:56.591
But she stumbled over Jacey's feet into Stuart.

12
00:00:58.851 --> 00:01:04.107
As Marv tried to help her up, Brooklyn's foot got caught in a bag of extra basketballs.

13
00:01:06.269 --> 00:01:09.311
Balls went spilling out and rolled onto the gym floor.

14
00:01:13.394 --> 00:01:15.016
no!" Brooklyn cried.

15
00:01:15.036 --> 00:01:16.517
"Sorry, Marv!"

16
00:01:17.318 --> 00:01:20.100
Marv rubbed his arm where Brooklyn had bumped into him.

17
00:01:20.120 --> 00:01:26.085
"It's okay, Brooklyn," he said as she scrambled to get the balls.

18
00:01:26.965 --> 00:01:28.307
His voice sounded tired.

19
00:01:28.327 --> 00:01:29.768
"They've got them."

20
00:01:30.932 --> 00:01:31.773
Marv was right.

21
00:01:32.333 --> 00:01:37.016
Jacey, Aaron, and a few other Whales were already scooping up the rolling balls.

22
00:01:40.138 --> 00:01:41.579
Brooklyn held the bag open.

23
00:01:41.599 --> 00:01:44.181
"Balls in here, guys."

24
00:01:45.042 --> 00:01:54.989
Then she heard loud moaning sounds and glanced Dirk held one of Coach Teagan's arms and was trying

25
00:01:55.009 --> 00:01:55.709
to help him up.

26
00:01:57.450 --> 00:01:59.312
But the coach was grimacing in pain.

27
00:02:01.076 --> 00:02:04.459
"Wait! Dirk, don't move him," Brooklyn said.

28
00:02:04.479 --> 00:02:06.200
"She's right.

29
00:02:06.280 --> 00:02:07.361
It could be serious."

30
00:02:07.821 --> 00:02:12.584
Marv pulled out his phone and called 911 for emergency medical help.

31
00:02:16.047 --> 00:02:18.749
Brooklyn hurried over to where Coach Teagan lay.

32
00:02:20.970 --> 00:02:22.631
He was wedged under the bleachers.

33
00:02:22.651 --> 00:02:27.235
"Ow!" Coach squeezed his eyes shut and gritted his teeth.

34
00:02:27.255 --> 00:02:28.736
"It hurts."

35
00:02:33.384 --> 00:02:37.606
Luckily for Coach Teagan, an ambulance arrived at the school in about eight minutes.

36
00:02:38.466 --> 00:02:43.228
No one on the Whales team seemed to be thinking about the game they'd lost anymore—they were all

37
00:02:43.308 --> 00:02:44.649
too worried about Coach.

38
00:02:45.489 --> 00:02:50.632
The players quickly shook hands with the Terriers, who then gathered up their gear and left to board

39
00:02:50.672 --> 00:02:51.192
their bus.

40
00:02:54.473 --> 00:03:01.828
Brooklyn and the rest of the team watched as two emergency medical workers attended to Coach Teagan.

41
00:03:01.848 --> 00:03:03.870
He struggled to get out from under the bleachers.

42
00:03:03.890 --> 00:03:07.192
"My wife needs me," he murmured.

43
00:03:07.212 --> 00:03:10.274
"Hold on, sir," a paramedic said.

44
00:03:10.294 --> 00:03:12.836
"We need to check your vital signs."

45
00:03:13.796 --> 00:03:19.060
While one medical worker put a cuff around Coach's arm to check his blood pressure, the other one

46
00:03:19.140 --> 00:03:21.061
set up a portable stretcher on wheels.

47
00:03:21.081 --> 00:03:27.045
"We're going to take you to Memorial Hospital for x-rays," she said.

48
00:03:28.186 --> 00:03:29.067
Coach groaned.

49
00:03:30.992 --> 00:03:32.673
"Someone had better call my wife!"

50
00:03:32.693 --> 00:03:38.855
"Coach and his wife are expecting babies any time now," Marv informed the medical workers.

51
00:03:38.875 --> 00:03:43.537
"Triplets." The paramedics raised their eyebrows in surprise.

52
00:03:43.557 --> 00:03:46.458
"Oh wow," the woman murmured.

53
00:03:47.939 --> 00:03:51.621
Brooklyn grabbed Jacey's arm and pointed to the other end of the bleachers.

54
00:03:51.641 --> 00:03:54.622
"I think Coach's phone flew that way.

55
00:03:55.042 --> 00:03:55.762
Let's find it!"

56
00:03:58.123 --> 00:04:03.365
The girls ran to look for the phone, and Brooklyn quickly spotted a black object lying on the

57
00:04:03.405 --> 00:04:05.465
floor. She picked it up.

58
00:04:06.326 --> 00:04:08.226
"This is just the phone's plastic cover.

59
00:04:08.806 --> 00:04:09.447
It's broken."

60
00:04:09.467 --> 00:04:12.828
"Here's the actual phone," Jacey said.

61
00:04:13.668 --> 00:04:16.108
She reached underneath the first row of bleachers.

62
00:04:16.128 --> 00:04:19.769
"Look. The screen is cracked."

63
00:04:20.650 --> 00:04:21.530
"That's not good."

64
00:04:21.850 --> 00:04:23.470
Brooklyn took the phone from Jacey.

65
00:04:23.490 --> 00:04:26.291
"I wonder if it still works."

66
00:04:27.151 --> 00:04:28.692
Suddenly it began ringing.

67
00:04:32.288 --> 00:04:35.089
"Hey!" Coach Teagan shouted from the stretcher.

68
00:04:35.109 --> 00:04:37.289
"That's my wife's ringtone!

69
00:04:37.710 --> 00:04:38.810
Brooklyn, answer it!"

70
00:04:40.190 --> 00:04:42.871
Brooklyn held the chipped phone carefully to her ear.

71
00:04:42.891 --> 00:04:46.292
"Hello?" Coach lifted his head.

72
00:04:46.312 --> 00:04:47.913
"She might be in labor!"

73
00:04:48.633 --> 00:04:49.313
"Hold still.

74
00:04:49.713 --> 00:04:50.413
Please, sir!"

75
00:04:50.833 --> 00:04:52.354
the emergency workers said.

76
00:04:53.394 --> 00:04:57.675
Brooklyn listened to the voice over the phone and then said, "I'll tell him."

77
00:04:58.516 --> 00:04:59.676
She ran over to Coach.

78
00:05:01.740 --> 00:05:03.441
"Your wife is in labor, Coach.

79
00:05:04.221 --> 00:05:06.623
A neighbor is driving her to the hospital right now."

80
00:05:06.643 --> 00:05:08.184
"Let's go!"

81
00:05:08.684 --> 00:05:09.865
Coach Teagan shouted.

82
00:05:09.885 --> 00:05:15.568
"We can meet your wife at the hospital, sir," the female paramedic said calmly.

83
00:05:15.588 --> 00:05:17.769
"There's no need to panic."

84
00:05:19.470 --> 00:05:21.131
"What's taking you two so long?"

85
00:05:21.551 --> 00:05:22.292
Coach snapped.

86
00:05:22.872 --> 00:05:24.433
"Let's move—now!"

87
00:05:25.393 --> 00:05:29.135
The Whales watched the medical workers roll Coach Teagan out of the gym.

88
00:05:32.108 --> 00:05:33.389
Brooklyn turned to Marv.

89
00:05:33.409 --> 00:05:36.111
"Will Coach be okay?"

90
00:05:36.551 --> 00:05:37.072
she asked.

91
00:05:37.092 --> 00:05:39.693
"It sounds like he hurt his hip.

92
00:05:40.194 --> 00:05:42.536
But I think he'll feel better once he sees his wife.

93
00:05:43.596 --> 00:05:46.378
The doctors and nurses will take good care of them both."

94
00:05:47.099 --> 00:05:48.260
Marv clapped his hands.

95
00:05:48.280 --> 00:05:53.383
"Okay, team, speaking of labor, we have a lot of work to do.

96
00:05:54.524 --> 00:05:55.945
Play-offs start next week.

97
00:05:56.746 --> 00:05:59.908
If we stick together, we can win the league championship!"

98
00:06:01.184 --> 00:06:03.785
Brooklyn watched Marv rub his beard nervously.

99
00:06:06.025 --> 00:06:08.386
Coach's injury was really bad timing.

100
00:06:09.646 --> 00:06:12.947
Marv was going to have to prepare the team for play-offs on his own.

101
00:06:12.967 --> 00:06:16.508
"Hey, Marv," she said slowly.

102
00:06:16.528 --> 00:06:19.409
"With Coach out, you're going to need some help.

103
00:06:20.069 --> 00:06:22.790
I was thinking—" "No way!"

104
00:06:23.190 --> 00:06:24.270
Dirk cut her off.

105
00:06:24.910 --> 00:06:26.591
"You're not coaching me, Brooklyn.

106
00:06:26.971 --> 00:06:28.591
Or anybody else on this team!"

107
00:06:29.572 --> 00:06:30.832
Brooklyn's face flushed.

108
00:06:31.540 --> 00:06:33.281
She looked around at the rest of the team.

109
00:06:34.402 --> 00:06:35.883
A few kids were looking down.

110
00:06:36.604 --> 00:06:38.125
Jacey was shaking her head.

111
00:06:39.286 --> 00:06:42.528
She shrugged and mouthed, "Sorry" to Brooklyn.

112
00:06:42.548 --> 00:06:45.910
"I know I can help," Brooklyn insisted.

113
00:06:45.930 --> 00:06:50.073
"I know this team, and I know a lot about basketball."

114
00:06:51.775 --> 00:06:52.976
"Like you helped today?"

115
00:06:53.636 --> 00:06:54.497
Dirk scowled.

116
00:06:54.517 --> 00:06:56.278
"We lost the game."

117
00:06:56.298 --> 00:06:58.139
"Okay, Dirk.

118
00:06:58.339 --> 00:06:58.940
That's enough.

119
00:06:59.488 --> 00:07:02.730
We'll discuss everything at practice on Monday," Marv said.

120
00:07:02.750 --> 00:07:05.671
"Now let's close up the gym."

121
00:07:06.491 --> 00:07:10.053
He went into the gym office and began clicking off the overhead lights.

122
00:07:14.295 --> 00:07:17.656
Dirk stood frowning in the shadows under the basketball net.

123
00:07:17.676 --> 00:07:21.838
"We're not much of a team without a head coach," he muttered.

124
00:07:21.858 --> 00:07:24.879
"You're right, Dirk," Jacey said.

125
00:07:24.899 --> 00:07:26.240
"This is bad."

126
00:07:27.356 --> 00:07:29.797
Aaron shrugged and pulled on his warm-up jacket.

127
00:07:29.818 --> 00:07:33.420
"We've got Marv," he said.

128
00:07:34.600 --> 00:07:38.222
His arms were so long that the jacket's sleeves barely reached his wrists.

129
00:07:38.242 --> 00:07:44.706
"My dad said everyone called him 'Marvelous Marv' when he played hoops in college, so Marv must know

130
00:07:44.746 --> 00:07:45.426
what he's doing."

131
00:07:45.446 --> 00:07:48.008
"You've got me too!"

132
00:07:48.468 --> 00:07:49.428
Brooklyn chimed in.

133
00:07:49.448 --> 00:07:53.511
"I've got a notebook filled with cool plays we can practice for the play-offs."

134
00:07:54.831 --> 00:07:55.572
Dirk snorted.

135
00:07:56.268 --> 00:07:58.269
"We won't make it very far in the play-offs.

136
00:07:58.629 --> 00:07:59.509
We're losers."

137
00:07:59.529 --> 00:08:02.630
"No, we're still a great team!"

138
00:08:03.050 --> 00:08:03.770
Brooklyn said.

139
00:08:04.630 --> 00:08:07.371
She grabbed a ball and dribbled it closer to Dirk.

140
00:08:10.432 --> 00:08:15.874
Maybe Dirk didn't like the idea of her coaching, but he loved basketball and the team.

141
00:08:15.894 --> 00:08:19.415
"I can win him over," Brooklyn thought.

142
00:08:20.215 --> 00:08:21.995
She suddenly held up the basketball.

143
00:08:22.015 --> 00:08:23.696
"Catch, Dirk!"

144
00:08:25.228 --> 00:08:27.050
Dirk's hands went up automatically.

145
00:08:27.730 --> 00:08:32.174
But just as Brooklyn tossed the ball, the gym went completely dark.

146
00:08:32.194 --> 00:08:36.698
"Ow!" shouted Dirk a second later.

147
00:08:36.718 --> 00:08:38.439
"My nose!"

148
00:08:39.240 --> 00:08:40.281
Brooklyn cringed.

149
00:08:40.301 --> 00:08:42.223
"Sorry, Dirk!"
